// Title: Potential Discovery Activity Using Find - Linux
// Sigma ID: 8344c0e5-5783-47cc-9cf9-a0f7fd03e6cf
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-12-28 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: discovery, T1083
// Description: Detects usage of "find" binary in a suspicious manner to perform discovery
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/SaiSathvik1/Linux-Privilege-Escalation-Notes
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_susp_find_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/find" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "-perm -4000" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-perm -2000" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-perm 0777" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-perm -222" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-perm -o w" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-perm -o x" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-perm -u=s" or ProcessCommandLine contains "-perm -g=s")
